### Sample 05 — many dispatcher nodes, one outbox table
### Start everything with .\run-nodes.ps1 first.
### Nodes run on 5005, 5006 and 5007; the shared receiver on 5100.

@node1 = http://localhost:5005
@node2 = http://localhost:5006
@node3 = http://localhost:5007
@receiver = http://localhost:5100

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### The nodes are identical apart from their identity.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Each index reports which node answered.
GET {{node1}}/

###
GET {{node2}}/

###
GET {{node3}}/

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Place work on ONE node, and watch all three dispatch it.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Start from a clean tally.
DELETE {{receiver}}/deliveries

### acceptedBy is node-1. It is routinely NOT the node that dispatches it.
POST {{node1}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "acme",
  "customerId": "cust-demo",
  "total": 99.50
}

### Send a few more, then watch the three node windows interleave.
POST {{node1}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "acme",
  "customerId": "cust-2",
  "total": 10.00
}

###
POST {{node1}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "acme",
  "customerId": "cust-3",
  "total": 20.00
}

### The assertion that matters: total must equal distinctOutboxIds.
### Anything else means a record went out twice.
GET {{receiver}}/deliveries/summary

### Everything received, with the attempt header on each.
GET {{receiver}}/deliveries

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### One table, three replicas.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Identical counters from every node, because there is only one table.
GET {{node1}}/outbox/stats

###
GET {{node2}}/outbox/stats

###
GET {{node3}}/outbox/stats

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Try this: close one node's window, then send more orders.
### The survivors absorb the backlog. total still equals distinctOutboxIds.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

###
POST {{node2}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "acme",
  "customerId": "cust-after-a-node-died",
  "total": 5.00
}

###
GET {{receiver}}/deliveries/summary
